+### (2.8) Clock-edge threshold noise ★
+
+**Statement**
+
+```
+t_j,threshold ≈ v_n,rms / S        where S = (dV/dt) at the receiver threshold
+```
+
+**Validity** — linear approximation of the edge through the threshold region. The
+relevant slew is at the **ADC clock pin**, not the oscillator's datasheet rise
+time. For a sine clock, `S_zero-crossing = 2π f_s V_p`. This is a delivered-clock
+term and **does not reduce intrinsic aperture jitter**.
+
+**Consequence for the Smart Guitar topology decision.** On a 3.3 V GPIO edge,
+even a pessimistic 10 ns rise with 20 mV of threshold noise yields ~61 ps:
+
+| Rise time | Slew | 1 mV | 5 mV | 20 mV |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 ns | 3.30 V/ns | 0.30 ps | 1.52 ps | 6.06 ps |
+| 2 ns | 1.65 V/ns | 0.61 ps | 3.03 ps | 12.1 ps |
+| 5 ns | 0.66 V/ns | 1.52 ps | 7.58 ps | 30.3 ps |
+| 10 ns | 0.33 V/ns | 3.03 ps | 15.2 ps | 60.6 ps |
+
+Against the ~1000 ps carried for a host fractional-N clock, threshold slew is an
+order of magnitude short of explaining it. **The Pi-master penalty is frequency
+synthesis, not edge quality**, so buffering or termination cannot rescue that
+topology — only codec-master can. Note the asymmetry: under codec-master the
+clock that determines the sample instant never crosses the header.
+
+**Class** `VENDOR` · **Source** requires citation (ADI RAQ-57, TI SBAA653)
+· **Code** `threshold_noise_jitter_s()`
 
