+### (3.5) Clock-versus-aperture de-embedding, and its conditioning ⚠
+
+**Statement**
+
+```
+t_ap = √(t_total² − t_clock@pin²)
+```
+
+with the clock characterized **at the ADC clock pin**, over an integration band
+matching the SNR integration band. Alternatively by substitution: measure
+`t_total,i²` against `t_clock,i²` for several clocks and fit — the intercept is
+`t_ap²`, and **the slope should be near 1**, which is the diagnostic that the
+model holds before the number is believed.
+
+**Conditioning.** RSS subtraction of similar quantities amplifies error by
+`1/(1−ρ²)` where `ρ = t_clock/t_total`:
+
+| ρ | t_ap/t_total | Amplification | 5% input error becomes |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 0.5 | 0.87 | 1.3× | 6.7% |
+| 0.7 | 0.71 | 2.0× | 9.8% |
+| 0.9 | 0.44 | 5.3× | 26% |
+| 0.95 | 0.31 | 10.3× | 51% |
+
+Keep the clock below roughly one-third to one-half of the total. If
+`t_total ≤ t_clock`, report total jitter or an upper bound and claim no aperture
+number.
+
+**Aperture jitter is conditional, not a fixed part property.** It varies with
+temperature, supply and reference noise, input frequency and amplitude, clock
+slew rate, and converter mode. A de-embedded value without its conditions is
+incomplete — structurally the same defect as a jitter figure without its
+integration limits (G7).
+
+**Not applicable to this instrument.** Both routes need phase-noise
+instrumentation at the pin or a substitutable clock; the board exposes neither.
+And the split would inform no decision: clock and converter are one purchasing
+unit.
+
+**Class** `VENDOR` · **Source** requires citation (ADI AN-501, TI SLYT422)
+
+### (3.6) Aperture delay — a different quantity
+
+| Quantity | Is | Measured by |
+|---|---|---|
+| Aperture **delay** | fixed mean offset, clock edge to sample instant | timing/phase measurement |
+| Aperture **jitter** | sample-to-sample variation of that offset | high-frequency FFT SNR |
+
+Delay is linear phase. In a two-channel transfer measurement it cancels **only if
+both channels share it** — verify, do not assume. The conflation is common enough
+that ADI gave it a tutorial: Kester, W. *MT-007: Aperture Time, Aperture Jitter,
+Aperture Delay Time — Removing the Confusion.* Analog Devices, 2008.
+
+**Class** `VENDOR` · **Source** MT-007 (op. cit.)
+· **Code** `ConverterSpec.aperture_delay_s`
 
