+### SNR integration convention
+
+Fixed for every test, or frequency-dependent comparisons are meaningless:
+
+```
+Window:  rectangular (none) for coherent captures
+Exclude: DC · bin M · mirror bin N-M · harmonics 2M..6M folded mod N
+         · identified deterministic spurs
+P_N   =  sum of remaining in-band bins
+SNR   =  10 log10(P_signal / P_N)
+```
+
+Including harmonics measures **SINAD**, not SNR. Report the two separately and
+never substitute one for the other. **SFDR** is a third quantity — the largest
+single spur relative to the carrier — and the only one that sees periodic
+contamination.
+
+### Source margin — a standing caveat, not a fixable condition
+
+Proper converter testing puts the source 10–15 dB cleaner than the device under
+test. **Loopback has zero margin**: the DAC and ADC are comparable parts, so a
+loopback figure is roughly 108 dB for a pair specified at 110 dB each. Every
+loopback result is a *system* measurement of two converters in series. Only T1's
+shorted input isolates the ADC. Do not report a loopback figure as a converter
+specification.
